  "site_name": "Bedelsford School",
  "epc_number": null,
  "pp_id": "PP-14121900",
  "subdivision_of_building": "- Front car park\n- Front boundary fencing and gates\n- Public footpath off Grange Road",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Alterations to Bedelsford School access and car park:\n- Adaptation of the public footpath and dropped kerbs adjacent to the existing vehicle entrance and exit to enable the widening of the vehicle access.\nDrop kerb application made 30/01/2026 ref:RBK-DROPK792697340\n- Demolition of three brick piers and small sections of adjoining walling, together with removal of the existing vehicle gates, to accommodate new, wider gates.\n- Installation of two new automatic HS Hyperion bi-folding trackless vehicle gates finished in green (RAL 6005).\n- Extension of the existing car park by converting an area of soft landscaping/soil. \n- Formation of a new pedestrian entrance through the existing retaining wall by creating a 1.2m opening, installing a 2m-high bow-top pedestrian gate with audio/visual access control, finished in green (RAL 6005).\n- Reconfiguration of car park circulation by reversing the entrance and exit arrangement to improve on-and-off-site traffic flow.\n- The implementation of additional parking bays (including a disabled parking bay), new directional paint markings, a new internal zebra crossing footpath, and two new surface mounted speed bumps. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with submitted arboricultural method statement. The approved measures shall be implemented prior to commencement of any work on site and maintained to the reasonable satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority until the completion of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy G7 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Prior to commencement of groundworks (excluding site investigations and demolition), a detailed drainage layout must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The layout should show the locations of the proposed SuDS and their connectivity to the discharge point, demonstrating compliance with the sustainable drainage hierarchy. The system shall be implemented, managed, and maintained according to the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure the development is made safe without increasing flood risk elsewhere in accordance with the National Planning Policy Framework (Planning and flood risk) and associated guidance, policy SI13 of the London Plan 2021, policy DM4 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012, and the National standards for sustainable drainage systems.\r",
    "No building hereby permitted shall be occupied until evidence (e.g. photographs and installation contract) demonstrating that the sustainable drainage scheme for the site has been completed in accordance with the approved details has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To ensure the development is made safe without increasing flood risk elsewhere in accordance with the National Planning Policy Framework (Planning and flood risk) and associated guidance, policy SI13 of the London Plan 2021, policy DM4 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012, and the National standards for sustainable drainage systems",
    "The gates hereby approved shall be installed to only open inwards away from the public highway and shall be permanently retained in this configuration for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To prevent obstruction of the adjacent footway and ensure the safety and efficient operation of the highway network for all users, in accordance with Policy T4 of the London Plan, Policies CS6 and DM8 of the Kingston Core Strategy, and the Residential Design SPD."
  ],
